  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "F-067-INDEX-CASE39",
      "classification": "明確なL10 cross-document index/trace omission。実FV CASE自体は存在するため、ここから未検証・false successとは推論しない。",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "path": "docs/helix-labo/L10-verification/functional-verification.md",
          "lines": "3231",
          "detail": "L10-LABO-067-CASE-39 is an individual LABO-067-AC-03 negative: normal observed inputs with L2-059 cost definition preserved, and only erroneous output changing the existing cost gate; expected rejection and LABO-output correction."
        },
        {
          "path": "docs/helix-labo/L3-requirements/business-requirements.md",
          "lines": "131",
          "detail": "BR index lists CASE 01/02/03a–g/04a–b/05–23/24–38; omits CASE-39."
        },
        {
          "path": "docs/helix-labo/L10-verification/business-verification.md",
          "lines": "131",
          "detail": "BV CASE index also ends 24–38; omits CASE-39."
        },
        {
          "path": "docs/helix-labo/L10-verification/nfr-verification.md",
          "lines": "180",
          "detail": "Functional CASE index also ends 24–38; omits CASE-39."
        },
        {
          "path": "docs/helix-labo/L3-requirements/functional-requirements.md",
          "lines": "1828,1832",
          "detail": "067 FR explicitly preserves adopted 059 quality/cost meaning and prohibits LABO-generated authority; AC-03 covers boundary/evidence."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "BR/BV/NFRV indexes understate the actual 067 FV scope by one explicit boundary case and can make indexed cross-document coverage look complete while the CASE-39 cost-gate preservation oracle is not listed. Direct FV case and FR context exist, so no demonstrated acceptance false-pass.",
      "minimum_followup": "If Root chooses to repair later, add CASE-39 to only the BR, BV, and NFRV index ranges (or add a narrow explicit reference) while preserving the existing CASE oracle and adopted L2-059 boundary; no new case/gate/meaning."
    },
    {
      "id": "F-059-CASE14-OWNER-AMBIGUITY",
      "classification": "補足read-only候補。revision不一致の否定oracle自体はあるが、異なるsource種別を一fixtureにまとめたため戻し先の根拠が不足/曖昧。false-successは示していない。",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "path": "docs/helix-labo/L2-requirements/labo-requirements.md",
          "revision": "f6dad2a33e24f000b87d7f09b8d40288257e74cc",
          "lines": "427–429",
          "detail": "L2-059:427 requires task, source, requirement and acceptance revisions/digests to be retained. L2-059:429 routes missing task/scope/assignment/result/receipt to OS or observation source and unknown quality/acceptance oracle to HARNESS/requirements owner; it does not explicitly assign all task-revision versus requirement-revision mismatches to one owner."
        },
        {
          "path": "docs/helix-labo/L10-verification/functional-verification.md",
          "revision": "37a8283be429c57f3706153ad522e7ad288fecc3",
          "lines": "2647",
          "detail": "CASE-14 changes “requirement/task revision” as one grouped revision condition and routes the comparison mismatch to HARNESS."
        },
        {
          "path": "docs/helix-labo/L3-requirements/functional-requirements.md",
          "revision": "37a8283be429c57f3706153ad522e7ad288fecc3",
          "lines": "1622",
          "detail": "AC-03 says only fixed L2-059:429 cause-specific existing source classes may be used; unknown if not identified."
        },
        {
          "path": "archive/legacy-generation-2026-09-14/root/docs/design/helix/L3-requirements/helix-bench-evaluation.md",
          "lines": "76–94",
          "detail": "Old R-03 keeps concrete runtime/model/effort/role versioned and avoids provider/model-name scoring; it does not define the current task-vs-requirement source-owner route."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The comparison is rejected, but the case cannot independently establish a correct return destination for both alternatives. Task/target revision provenance may be OS/observation-source input; requirement/acceptance contract version belongs to the contract/requirements source. Fixed L2-059 does not give enough basis to hardcode the same HARNESS return for both.",
      "minimum_followup": "If repaired, retain CASE-14 as a compatibility/index reference or split into two single-field cases: task/target revision mismatch and requirement/acceptance revision mismatch. Keep both comparisons unmeasured; route only by an explicitly fixed existing source category, and preserve unknown if individual owner is not identified. No new owner/approval or threshold."
    }
  ],
  "review_results": {
    "064": "L2/L11 fixed source adopted; Stage5 semantic mapping reviewed across BR/FR/NFR/BV/FV/NFRV. No new false-success found. Historical residual CASE-22 lacks explicit return destination is retained as a prior residual, not upgraded to blocker. CASE-03a/24 overlap is known and is not counted twice. All fixtures synthetic/unexecuted.",
